# A bare PointsAt assignment needs a pointer move beside it and an allowlist entry - declaring a tooltip is not raising it.
# PointsAt says WHICH dossier the node shows; OnFocusVisual is what makes the game draw it. One without the other reviews correctly and never appears.
# Prefer GraphNodes.SectionsFor(vtable, …) or an AgeWidgets.Point/PointAt helper, which wire both. Bare aims belong to the aimless cases only.
#
# Generated by ES2ACCESS_LINT_REGENERATE=1; format: path | count | source line.
#

ES2Access/Screens/DropListScreen.cs | 1 | vtable.PointsAt = () => AgeWidgets.Raw(under);

